<p>Brazilian Supreme Court Justice Alexandre de Moraes blocked implementation of a law that could reduce prison sentences for former President Jair Bolsonaro and other defendants, pending a full court review of constitutional challenges. Bolsonaro was sentenced to 27 years in prison in September after the Supreme Court found he had plotted to stay in power after losing the 2022 election to Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva. The measure, described in Brazilian coverage as the Lei da Dosimetria, applied to people convicted over the coup plot and the Jan. 8 attacks. It would shorten waiting periods for sentence-reduction requests, though defense lawyers would still need the Supreme Court to recalculate sentences in each case.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/nXaUOac4hoDhvSWaGH8GpYNyga25QQUsCsGdJUL2odVGTiZGJrHei18ksXKvVqtdDvN49Jaaycg32zPQ1Upplwqp0XDZndAyZ0GLquXLazAYlEDr-FA_QSd5qCpAb_bGD_5Ltb6-DQ' alt='Former Brazilian President Jair Bolsonaro.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Release timing: The Straits Times said the bill could have made Bolsonaro eligible for release in 2028, while n-tv said his sentence could be cut to two years.</li><li>Legal challenges: Two Brazilian political parties and the Brazilian Press Association, known as ABI, filed separate challenges to the bill this week.</li><li>Veto politics: CNA, citing AFP, said a conservative-majority Congress passed the measure and Bolsonaro allies later led the override of Lula&#x27;s veto.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/9/brazil-judge-bars-law-that-could-reduce-bolsonaros-27-year-prison-sentence'>Brazil judge bars law that could reduce Bolsonaro’s 27-year prison sentence</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-judge-suspends-law-that-reduces-bolsonaro-s-jail-term/a-77107420'>Brazil judge suspends law that reduces Bolsonaro&#x27;s jail term</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/brazil-supreme-court-justice-susp